## Stages and Gates

1. **Spec.** Ordinary spec work. Write verification notes and impact cells when the
   thought occurs. Use spikes and sketch models to surface surprises early. Stay here
   as long as surprises keep coming.
2. **The Bridge.** System description, the claims sweep, `claims.md`.
3. **Formalize.** `model.rs`, one feature at a time.
4. **Implement and prove.** Write each harness alongside its operation. Write
   discoveries back before continuing.

The gates between them are in `docs/verification-strategy.md`. Do not pass one that is
not met.

### Reentry
Reopening something after formal items rest on it is an event. Mark it `REOPENED`, run
`tools/check rests-on <item>`, read what depends on it, then discuss. Update everything
downstream in the same sitting. See "Reentry" in the verification strategy.

---

## Keep Docs in Sync

- Update the spec when reality changes. A stale spec misleads.
- A formal item's home is its Rust file. Never restate it in markdown; refer by ID.
- References point upstream only. Never edit an earlier document to point forward.
- Never record by hand what `tools/check` can compute, including verification status.
- Run `tools/check` before closing any gate or reentry.
